# The chart IS the repository root: a builder publishes Chart.yaml, values.yaml, values.schema.json
# and templates/ there. Without this file `helm package .` packs the repository with the chart —
# .git/, .github/, the README. Every entry below belongs to the repository, not to the chart.
#
# The registration file, compositiondefinition.yaml, is NOT listed: it ships inside the package.
# The organisation's helm index takes the archive GHCR holds and refuses a blueprint whose archive
# does not register itself (krateo-blueprints/charts PUBLISHING.md, rules 1 and 3), so release-oci
# stamps it with the version and checks it is there before it pushes. Helm never renders a file at
# the chart root, so shipping it installs nothing.
#
# Files that exist only at the root are anchored with a leading slash. Helm matches a name without a
# slash at ANY depth, so an unanchored `*.tgz` would also drop charts/<dependency>.tgz and the package
# would fail ("found in Chart.yaml, but missing in charts/ directory").
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.helmignore
.krateoignore
/dist/
/*.tgz
/README.md
/CHANGELOG.md
# A blueprint's status projection (the <chart>-status RESTAction + its apiRef rows): the portal's Install
# step applies it beside the registration file, so it belongs to the repository.
/status-projection.json
